course: dictionary
lesson: 661
title: A word from another language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words in a dictionary do not come from English at all. «Bai» is one of them. It is a Mandarin word, and it sounds like the English word "by" or "bye". Sounds alone do not tell you the meaning, so check the dictionary.
explain: In Mandarin, the tone, or how your voice goes up or down, can change the meaning. «Bái» means white, «bǎi» means hundred, and «bài» is a third tone. The same sound can mean different things.
explain: Bai is also a name. In a story you may meet «A legend says Li Bai drowned reaching for the Moon's reflection, but he probably died of illness.» Here Bai is part of a person's name, not a colour or a number. Context helps you see which meaning fits.
fact: Bai is not an English word. It is a Mandarin word, the language spoken in China.
fact: «Bái» (白) means white.
fact: «Bǎi» (百) means hundred, as in «yī bǎi», one hundred.
fact: Bai is a Chinese family name. It is also the name of an ethnic group of people in Yunnan, China.
fact: Tone marks show how your voice moves, and in Mandarin they can change a word's meaning.
exercise: «Yī bǎi» means one hundred. In this phrase, bǎi means what? | Poet | *Hundred | Moon | White
exercise: «A legend says Li Bai drowned reaching for the Moon's reflection, but he probably died of illness.» In this sentence, Bai is a what? | A number | A colour | A ball game | *Part of a person's name
exercise: Is bai an English word? | Yes, it means hundred | Yes, it means white | Yes, it is a common English word | *No, it is a Mandarin word that sounds like "by"
test: In Mandarin, what does «bái» mean? | *White | Hundred | Family | Poet
test: The word for hundred is written 百. How is it written in pinyin? | *bǎi | bài | Yunnan | bái
exam: In Mandarin, why does the tone matter? | It shows the word is a name | *It can change the meaning of the same sounds | It makes the word louder | It means the word is English
